WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.666
- So Maks and Val,

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:04.020
so out of your many years
on "Dancing with the Stars,"

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.490
who were your most memorable partners?

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.323
Who do you think?

00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:07.156
Not to diss the others,

00:00:07.156 --> 00:00:08.850
just who's somebody that stood out?

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.780
- My wife.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.687
- Oh, well, (beep)

00:00:10.687 --> 00:00:12.180
(laughing)

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.020
Good answer.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:13.853
- [Val] Yeah, my wife.

00:00:13.853 --> 00:00:14.686
- This is why you're still married.

00:00:14.686 --> 00:00:15.519
Good answer.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:16.352
- Thank you.

00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:17.643
(clapping)

00:00:17.643 --> 00:00:18.540
- It's a pleasure,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.710
and one of the biggest pleasures

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.020
is the dynamic personalities

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.880
and people that you go
through this process with,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.990
and it's,

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.790
I don't wanna say a gauntlet,

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.790
but it is something that
really brings people together.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.350
And one of the partners that I had

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.960
the privilege to be a pro partner

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.974
with on "Dancing with
the Stars" was Zendaya.

00:00:35.974 --> 00:00:36.980
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.122
Oh yeah, I forgot.

00:00:38.122 --> 00:00:39.538
(clapping)

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:41.040
She was young, right?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.087
- [Val] She was 16,

00:00:42.087 --> 00:00:44.580
and she was just kind
of trying to transition

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.120
out of the Disney star.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.190
And yeah, the rest is history.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.190
- Yeah, that's a crazy career, that one.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.060
She's so talented.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:54.900
- [Priyanka] So talented.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.160
- So Maks, does it ever bother you

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.650
that Val won twice and you know,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.483
you won once?

00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:00.685
I'm just pointing it out.

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:01.518
(laughing)
Just pointing it out.

00:01:01.518 --> 00:01:02.351
- It doesn't bother me because,

00:01:02.351 --> 00:01:04.017
- [Kelly] Does he ever rub it in?

00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:04.850
- Because he won twice,

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.270
my wife won twice,

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.560
His wife won twice.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.700
- [Priyanka] Oh my gosh.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.773
- [Kelly] Just holding it down.

00:01:09.773 --> 00:01:11.489
- My 6 year old was

00:01:11.489 --> 00:01:13.380
in my wife's belly,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.880
I guess when they won together,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.177
so he has half a trophy.

00:01:16.177 --> 00:01:17.010
(laughing)

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.540
I only have one in 17 seasons.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.880
But, I gotta say that my best partner

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.680
was probably the show itself.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.301
- Oh, yeah. Good answer.

00:01:24.301 --> 00:01:27.000
- 17 seasons of incredible opportunities.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.920
Look at us now type of thing.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.971
- So we're grateful.

00:01:29.971 --> 00:01:30.804
- [Kelly] That's a great answer, yeah.

00:01:30.804 --> 00:01:31.862
(clapping)

00:01:31.862 --> 00:01:33.720
'Cause people don't know,

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.553
I don't know.

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:35.386
That's one of the reasons why I love

00:01:35.386 --> 00:01:36.540
being part of "The Voice" too.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:37.980
It does that for other artists.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.150
Not only the artists you're working with,

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:39.983
but also the coaches.

00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:41.820
It kind of lets you kind of reinvent

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.780
yourself too in a way.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.880
And that's really cool
how shows allow people

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.530
to really stretch their creative muscles

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.820
and be noticed in a different way.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:48.653
- But it's also,

00:01:48.653 --> 00:01:50.280
what we kind of take for granted sometimes

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.050
is the people that we gathered

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.030
in those shows are your core fans,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.717
your core audience.

00:01:55.717 --> 00:01:56.880
It's the support system that you have.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.220
Nowadays, social media craziness.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.290
We can rely on people we've never met.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.550
I don't even know where they live,

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.680
but I can always get this nice message

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.940
that makes me feel like,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:06.773
you know what?

00:02:06.773 --> 00:02:07.606
I'm gonna go out.

00:02:07.606 --> 00:02:09.960
I'm gonna do it again, no
matter what the critics say.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.586
'Cause there's people that
really love your work.

00:02:11.586 --> 00:02:12.480
- That's why you're really here.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.470
All the people supporting you?

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.940
- Yeah, and popcorn.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:15.773
- And popcorn.

00:02:15.773 --> 00:02:16.819
- And popcorn.

00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:17.652
Thank you for grabbing from mine.

00:02:17.652 --> 00:02:18.485
Okay, thanks.

00:02:18.485 --> 00:02:19.885
- This is the winner for me.

00:02:19.885 --> 00:02:20.940
- This is really good.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.380
I never had that before.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.213
- I'm gonna send you some.

00:02:23.213 --> 00:02:24.046
- Oh no, I know.

00:02:24.046 --> 00:02:24.927
Don't you worry, I'll buy it.

00:02:24.927 --> 00:02:27.600
- Get it at Walmart and
Vons and Albertsons.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.783
- [Kelly] I like to support
you, I'm gonna buy it.

